&& L0 -- does SETPATH WORKSPACES redirect the workspace catalog?
&& AIF-078 lifecycle lane. Read-only against production: it opens the
&& production catalog to COUNT it and never writes to it.
&& Every path is spelled in full and unambiguously, but through the ENGINE-OWNED
&& variables `&_DATA` and `&_TMP` rather than one machine's drive letter. The
&& probe's point survives: nothing here leans on path RESOLUTION to find a target,
&& which is the thing under test.
&& AMENDED 2026-09-12. This line read "Every path is absolute and spelled in full,
&& on purpose." -- a STATED REASON, which OI-017's rule allows. It does not hold.
&& L1VERIFY, three days later in this same lane, reached the opposite conclusion
&& and called the machine path "OI-017's shape, here in the lifecycle lane's own
&& tooling" (fd0d6ef40 established `&_TMP`). L0 predated that and was never swept,
&& so the lane ruled both ways until now.

ECHO === production catalog, BEFORE ===
USE &_DATA\workspaces\WORKSPACES.dbf
COUNT

ECHO === redirect to scratch, then mint one workspace ===
SETPATH WORKSPACES &_TMP\wscat_l0
WORKSPACE NEW L0PROBE

ECHO === scratch catalog -- expect 1 ===
USE &_TMP\wscat_l0\WORKSPACES.dbf
COUNT

ECHO === restore, then production AFTER -- must equal BEFORE ===
SETPATH WORKSPACES &_DATA\workspaces
USE &_DATA\workspaces\WORKSPACES.dbf
COUNT

ECHO === THE FORK: does a SHIPPED posture resolve under a redirect? ===
SETPATH WORKSPACES &_TMP\wscat_l0
WORKSPACE LOAD cascade_all

ECHO === restore and confirm the slot really came back ===
SETPATH WORKSPACES &_DATA\workspaces
SETPATH
